Subject: [PATCH 3312/3799] soh: rename func_800FCA18 -> SystemHeap_DeleteArray

Name source: DEDUCED from the code (confidence HIGH) -- zeldaret/oot
leaves this symbol address-named too, so there is no upstream name to adopt.
Reason: destructs the elements from the end backwards and frees the block
Defined in soh/src/code/system_heap.c.

Tagged [LLM:HIGH] at the definition, every declaration and every call site, so a
reader meeting the name anywhere knows it is inferred.
---
 soh/src/code/system_heap.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/soh/src/code/system_heap.c b/soh/src/code/system_heap.c
index 75b48de80..66ec8bf4a 100644
--- a/soh/src/code/system_heap.c
+++ b/soh/src/code/system_heap.c
@@ -150,7 +150,8 @@ void* SystemHeap_NewArray(void* blk, u32 nBlk, u32 blkSize, arg3_800FC948 arg3)
     return blk;
 }
 
-void func_800FCA18(void* blk, u32 nBlk, u32 blkSize, arg3_800FCA18 arg3, s32 arg4) {
+// LLM generated name (HIGH), was func_800FCA18: destructs the elements from the end backwards and frees the block
+void SystemHeap_DeleteArray(void* blk, u32 nBlk, u32 blkSize, arg3_800FCA18 arg3, s32 arg4) {
     uintptr_t pos;
     uintptr_t end;
     s32 masked_arg2;
